# SMTP password encryption key for this installation.
# Copy this file to smtp.key in the same directory, then replace the
# placeholder line with one line of key material. Do not commit smtp.key.
#
# Generate a key on the server:
#   php -r "echo base64_encode(random_bytes(32)), PHP_EOL;"
#
# Or set the environment variable TAPSTEMCO_SMTP_KEY to that same value
# and do not create smtp.key. The environment variable is used first.
#
# This example is not a valid key. The application will refuse to store
# an SMTP password until a real key is installed. Do not put a mailbox
# password in this file.
REPLACE_WITH_OUTPUT_OF_THE_COMMAND_ABOVE
